25-04-28\nValid as Of: 2025-04-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 994 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Notifications\nDescription: Using the notifications feature in SAP Build Process Automation, you can now send notifications to recipient groups also apart from recipient users. See  Enable Notifications  Manage and Personalize your Notifications.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-28\nValid as Of: 2025-04-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 995 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Outbox Feature Available in the SAP Task Center Web App\nDescription: A new Outbox feature is available in the Web app for users to view their completed tasks, along with their details, comments, and attachments. For more information, see SAP Task Center Web App - Outbox.  A new property tc.outbox must be set by administrators to enable the Outbox tab in the Web app. For more information, see SAP Task Center Global Settings.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-28\nValid as Of: 2025-04-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 996 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Electronic Document Error Explanations\nDescription: The Manage Electronic Documents app now enables natural language interaction with Joule, making it easier to understand electronic document exchange errors. You can ask Joule for error explanations and recommended resolution steps. By providing detailed insights, SAP Joule helps you understand the root cause of errors and offers guidance on corrective actions.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-24\nValid as Of: 2025-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 997 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Analytical Insights Capability in Joule with SAP Analytics Cloud\nDescription: Joule, powered by SAP Analytics Cloud, now allows you to explore your data and gain insights into your business, in a natural, conversational experience. Using familiar business terms, simply ask your question, and the analytical insights capability will instantly provide answers about your data as simple charts and metrics.For more information on this capability, see Analytical Insights with SAP Analytics Cloud.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Analytics\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-24\nValid as Of: 2025-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 998 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Transactional Capabilities Now Supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now provides the following transactional capability for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition, Finance:    Create Fixed Asset Master Data    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-24\nValid as Of: 2025-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 999 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Developer's Guide\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Connect to Remote Systems\nDescription: There is a new page explaining how to connect to remote systems, the different use cases you might have, and what is the best approach for each use case.  See Connecting to Remote Systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-25\nValid as Of: 2025-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1000 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription: We've updated the map plug-in in the marketplace. To", " the best approach for each use case.  See Connecting to Remote Systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-25\nValid as Of: 2025-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1000 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription: We've updated the map plug-in in the marketplace. To use the new component, first install it from the Marketplace. Migrate from the Embedded map view (beta) component to the new Embedded map view component.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-25\nValid as Of: 2025-04-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3551 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extraction of Descriptions from Columns\nDescription: We’ve fixed an issue with extracting description values from columns.  SAP Document AI now extracts the complete content of large column cells containing descriptions of numbers or quantities, for example.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-05\nValid as Of: 2024-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3552 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extraction of Line Items\nDescription: We’ve fixed an issue with extracting line items.  If the template returns the extraction result invalid, but the AI returns the extraction result valid for the same line item, the final result is now valid when SAP Document AI merges the two results.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-05\nValid as Of: 2024-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3553 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Get Templates Endpoint\nDescription: The limit parameter of the Get Templates endpoint is now independent of the order parameter.   To apply the limit parameter, you no longer need to specify a value for order.  See Get Template.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-05\nValid as Of: 2024-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3554 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Model Used for Extraction\nDescription: The Document API now includes information about the model used for extraction. As a result, you can see whether SAP Document AI used a template or AI to extract information from a particular field.  See Get Result.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-05\nValid as Of: 2024-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3555 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Location for Schema Configuration Feature on UI\nDescription: You now call up the Schema Configuration feature of the SAP Document AI basic UI directly from the navigation bar on the left of the screen.  See Create Schema.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-05\nValid as Of: 2024-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3556 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for New Actions - Claim, Release, Forward\nDescription: Claim, Release and Forward are now available for SAP S/4HANA, SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition and SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition tasks.  For more information, see Inline Decision Options and Predefined Decision Reasons.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-05\nValid as Of: 2024-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3557 ---\nComponent: Cloud Application Programming Model\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: January Release\nDescription: The January release of the SAP Cloud Application Programming Model is now available.   Highlights:    Open Telemetry Plugin  Programmatic Outboxing of Services  Support for Spring Boot 3.2  … and much more.  See January 2024 release for the CAP framework.   Action: We recommend to adapt the new versions as soon as possible, see Managing Dependencies.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-02-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3558 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription: The microservice now supports address validation in Paraguay and Venezuela to the house number level. See Country Coverage for more information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-02-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3559 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Actions - Flattening Object Structure\nDescription: You can now use the new flattening feature, allowing you to streamline complex API responses by condensing them into a single-level structure. This feature enhances readability and simplifies data processing for a more efficient and intuitive user experience.  See:   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-02\nValid as Of: 2024-02-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3560 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: For SAP S/4HANA: BC Set for credit agency Creditreform CH\nDescription: For the credit agency Creditreform CH a BC set is now available:   3413168 : BC Set for Creditreform CH  The BC set for Creditreform CH contains only rating procedures for Business products. For Consumer products, you have to maintain your own rating procedures.  More information: Configure Rating Procedures  (Log on", " Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: For SAP S/4HANA: BC Set for credit agency Creditreform CH\nDescription: For the credit agency Creditreform CH a BC set is now available:   3413168 : BC Set for Creditreform CH  The BC set for Creditreform CH contains only rating procedures for Business products. For Consumer products, you have to maintain your own rating procedures.  More information: Configure Rating Procedures  (Log on with your SAP ID to access this document.)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-02\nValid as Of: 2024-02-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 381 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration of API Management with SAP Cloud ALM for Centralized Developer Hub Certificate Expiry Monitoring\nDescription: You can now integrate API Management with SAP Cloud Application Lifecycle Management (CALM). By leveraging CALM's health monitoring capabilities, you can configure automated email notifications to be sent when centralized Developer Hub certificates approach their expiry date. This enables proactive certificate management and helps prevent unexpected disruptions. For more information, see Monitor the Health of Certificates Using SAP Cloud ALM  SAP API Management customers choose: Monitor the Health of Certificates Using SAP Cloud ALM  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 382 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Message Queues No Longer Required\nDescription: Cloud Integration's message queue functionality is no longer a requirement for working with Data Space Integration.For more details on the onboarding, see Preparatory Steps.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 383 ---\nComponent: Data Space Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription: The following are the latest versions in Data Space Integration:      Data Space Integration: 1.11.*      Increment: 2506      Tractus-X Eclipse Dataspace Connector: 0.7.6      FOSS Eclipse Dataspace Components: 0.7.2      See also the Release Notes of Catena-X. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 384 ---\nComponent: Event Mesh\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Message Monitoring\nDescription: You can check the various parameters for a message in a queue. See Monitor Event Mesh.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 385 ---\nComponent: Event Mesh\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Role Collection\nDescription: A new role collection, EventMeshBusinessExpert is available. See Configuring User Access to SAP Integration Suite.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 386 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Combining Overlay MAGs with Pretransformation\nDescription: You can now combine an overlay MAG with pretransformation. The following scenarios are possible:     Base MAG with PTS and overlay MAG without pretransformation  Base MAG with PTS and overlay MAG with modified pretransformation  Base MAG without PTS and overlay MAG with pretransformation  Disable pretransformation of base MAG without pretransformation of overlay MAG (Indirectly)    To learn about these different scenarios, see Working with an Overlay Mapping Guideline.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Working with an Overlay Mapping Guideline.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 387 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Download MAG Simulation Results as EDI Flat File\nDescription: You can now download the result of a MAG simulation as an EDI flat file. You can only use this additional option if the target message is an EDI message from one of the type systems ASC X12, Odette, TRADACOMS, UN/EDIFACT or one of its subsets.  After a simulation has run, instead of choosing   Download simulation result, open the download menu. There, choose Download as EDI Flat File.  See Simulating a Mapping Guideline.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Simulating a Mapping Guideline.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 388 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Harmonization of User Interface for Code Value Mappings with 1:1 and n:1 Cardinality\nDescription: The user interface for code value mappings for 1:1 and n:1 cardinality has been harmonized.  See Code Value Mapping.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Code Value Mapping. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 389 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 2.2.*    Increment: 2506    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle:", " \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-27\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 389 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 2.2.*    Increm